course: dictionary
lesson: 6745
title: A people, a lake, a name
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Oneida starts with a capital letter because it is a proper noun, the name of one particular thing. It can name a people, their language, a lake or a town. Read the words around it to find out which one is meant.
explain: «The Haudenosaunee Confederacy united the Mohawk, Oneida, Onondaga, Cayuga and Seneca.» Here Oneida is one nation in a group of nations, so it means the people, not the lake.
explain: When Oneida is followed by a place, like Oneida Lake in New York State, it is a place name. Those places were named after the Oneida people.
fact: Oneida is the name of a Native American people, one of the Six Nations of the Haudenosaunee.
fact: The Haudenosaunee are also called the Iroquois Confederacy.
fact: Oneida is also the name of the Oneida people's language.
fact: Oneida Lake is in New York State, and some towns are named after the Oneida people.
fact: In the American Revolution the Oneida sided with the Americans. Today they have lands in New York and Wisconsin.
exercise: «The Haudenosaunee Confederacy united the Mohawk, Oneida, Onondaga, Cayuga and Seneca.» In this sentence, what is Oneida? | A town with a big square | *A people, one of the nations of the Haudenosaunee | A lake in New York State | The name of a river
exercise: Oneida Lake lies in New York State. What does Oneida mean in this name? | A kind of fish | A petrol station | *A place name, given after the Oneida people | The Scots word for grey rain
exercise: «The Oneida sided with the Americans in the American Revolution.» What does sided mean? | *Took the side of and supported them | Ran away from them | Built a fort for them | Fought against them
test: Why does Oneida start with a capital letter? | *Because it is a proper noun, the name of a particular people or place | Because it is always at the start of a sentence | Because it is a long word | Because it is a colour
test: «The Haudenosaunee Confederacy had a Great Law of Peace; clan mothers chose chiefs and could remove them.» Who chose the chiefs? | Men only | *Clan mothers | The Americans | The chiefs chose themselves
exam: Which best describes the Oneida? | A Scottish word for grey, wet weather | A petrol station in Australia | A kind of dog | *A Native American people, one of the Six Nations of the Haudenosaunee, from what is now New York State
